cut — Extract columns/characters

Used to extract specific parts from each line.

Suppose:

101,Sunil,Java,50000
102,Ravi,AWS,60000
103,Amit,React,55000

File:

employees.csv
Extract first column
cut -d',' -f1 employees.csv

Output:

101
102
103
Extract second column
cut -d',' -f2 employees.csv

Output:

Sunil
Ravi
Amit
Extract multiple columns
cut -d',' -f1,2 employees.csv

Output:

101,Sunil
102,Ravi
103,Amit
Extract a range
cut -d',' -f1-3 employees.csv

Output:

101,Sunil,Java
102,Ravi,AWS
103,Amit,React

Option	Meaning
-d	 delimiter
-f	field/column
-c	characters
-b	bytes

